  "rule": "Each legend motif (left of the divider) whose colour has both a marker row (on the left/right frame border) and a marker column (on the top/bottom frame border) is stamped into the frame interior, centred on every crossing of those rows and columns. The motif is then erased from the legend. Stamps are painted from the lowest legend motif upward, so the higher legend motif wins where stamps overlap. Motifs that lack either a row marker or a column marker stay in the legend.",
  "scope": "Supported in random scenes: legend width 3-5; height 9-30; frame width 9..(29-legend_width), total width up to 30; random distinct frame, divider and motif colours; 2-5 legend motifs; 1-4 stamped motifs, each with 1-2 marker rows and 1-2 marker columns (several copies, possibly overlapping each other); unstamped motifs with no markers, row markers only, or column markers only; 0-2 distractor marker colours with no motif, placed on rows, columns, both, or a single top/bottom edge. The distractor colour may equal the divider colour. Overlaps between different stamps are resolved by legend order. Not supported: stamps that reach the frame border or leave the grid; even-sized motif bounding boxes (centring is defined, but such shapes are not sampled); markers on the frame corners in random scenes (the fixtures' odd corner cell is reproduced only through explicit parameters); two motifs of the same colour.",
  "constraints": [
    "Background 0 is strictly the most common colour of the input.",
    "The frame colour strictly dominates the frame border cells.",
    "The divider is the leftmost full uniform non-background column. Legend motifs are at most 5 tall, so no legend column is uniform.",
    "Motif colours are distinct and differ from the frame colour and the divider colour.",
    "Each motif occupies a distinct top row, so the legend paint order is unambiguous.",
    "Each edge cell carries at most one marker colour. Left and right side markers are mirrored. Motif column markers are mirrored on top and bottom.",
    "Stamped copies lie entirely within the frame interior.",
    "Every stamped colour remains visible in the output interior, and at least one motif is stamped, so the output is never identical to the input."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
